<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- THE daily pipeline (2026-09-14 — no longer a safety net). The machine is
     realistically only on in the evening, so the 06:10 (US) and 16:50 (HK)
     launchd jobs were removed on 2026-09-14; these two guarded evening slots
     are now the ONLY daily runs for both lanes. At 20:30 HKT the HK lane's
     same-day session is complete (close 16:00, bars storable from 16:10); the
     US lane processes the PREVIOUS US session (closed 04:00/05:00 HKT that
     morning) — lag 1 by construction, admissible under the promptness gate.

     20:30 HKT is the primary slot; 23:03 HKT is the second chance for an
     evening the first slot missed (launchd has no memory of calendar slots
     that elapsed while the machine was off — architecture §5.1).

     23:03 HKT is safe for both lanes ONLY because of the 2026-09-13
     session-close filter (quant-core sessionClosed, applied at the
     fetch/upsert boundary in screen:daily): at 23:03 HKT the US session is in
     progress (open 21:30 HKT in EDT / 22:30 in EST), and the filter guarantees
     Yahoo's still-forming bar never enters the store, so the guard screens the
     previous COMPLETED US session. Without that filter this slot would poison
     the sample it protects.

     scripts/daily-catchup.sh runs a lane only when ops:catchup reports it is
     behind, so a healthy evening is a no-op rather than a duplicate run.
     Since 2026-09-14 the guard no longer trusts the store alone: it PROBES
     the provider for the newest completed session (first 3 universe names,
     sessionClosed filter), so a power-off day — store never fetched, nothing
     to compare — can no longer read as "up to date" (the 2026-09-14 incident:
     powered off until 20:05 HKT, HK's session nearly lost while every surface
     reported healthy).
     PATH is exported by the script itself (see its header), as in daily-chain.sh —
     every other plist here relies on the script, and a plist PATH is easy to get
     wrong silently: the first version of this one named ~/.local/share/pnpm, which
     does not exist on this machine. Install: scripts/launchd/install.sh -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.agentic-trading.daily-catchup</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Users/yongouyang/projects/agentic-trading/scripts/daily-catchup.sh</string>
  </array>
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <array>
    <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>20</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>23</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>3</integer></dict>
  </array>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/Users/yongouyang/projects/agentic-trading/logs/daily-catchup.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/yongouyang/projects/agentic-trading/logs/daily-catchup.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
